Theme definitions now store their colors in two JSON registry fields, `color_groups` and `block_themes`, replacing the per-color fields (`primary_color_light`, `font_family_primary` and the like). Existing themes keep their colors: until the upgrade step (profile version 1002) runs, their Color Groups are derived from the old records, and the upgrade step then stores them as Color Groups. `font_family_secondary` and the event/file/image colors have no Color Group equivalent and are still stored and served as before. Theme updates still accept the old per-color fields, and GenericSetup profiles that set them on `ISCVLTThemeDefinition` (as the PortalBrasil Intranet does) still install on new sites; the control panel now serves `ISCVLTThemeSchema`, which has only the new fields. @Humanaice
